        "original_id": "f3d4b968-dd14-5700-8155-4a892c1f97c2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Gundestrup cauldron\n- Cultures: La Tène culture\n- Places: Europe, La Tène, Lake Neuchâtel, Switzerland\n\nFacts:\n- In 1857, thousands of objects were discovered at the archaeological site of La Tène on the north side of Lake Neuchâtel in Switzerland after the water level dropped.\n- The La Tène culture was a European Iron Age culture named after the archaeological site of La Tène in Switzerland.\n- The Gundestrup cauldron is the largest known example of European Iron Age silver work.\n- The Gundestrup cauldron has a diameter of 69 cm and a height of 42 cm.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "bf4d0c71-851f-5e58-9bb8-325eda1a8859",
        "text": "Page: Gundestrup cauldron. Sentence: The cauldron is the largest known example of European Iron Age silver work (diameter: 69 cm ; height: 42 cm ).\nPage: La Tène culture. Sentence: The La Tène culture ( ; ] ) was a European Iron Age culture named after the archaeological site of La Tène on the north side of Lake Neuchâtel in Switzerland, where thousands of objects had been deposited in the lake, as was discovered after the water level dropped in 1857.",
